i</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Serafino</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Effect of extremely low frequency (ELF) magnetic field exposure on morphological and biophysical properties of human lymphoid cell line (Raji).</article-title><source>Biochim Biophys Acta</source><volume>1357</volume><fpage>281</fpage><lpage>290</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9268052</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000395-Smith1"><label>56</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>OM</given-names></name><name><surname>Goodman</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Greenebaum</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Tipnis</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>1991</year><article-title>An increase in the negative surface charge of U937 cells exposed to a pulsed magnetic field.</article-title><source>Bioelectromagnetics</source><volume>12</volume><fpage>197</fpage><lpage>202</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1854356</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000395-Ikehara1"><label>57</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ikehara</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamaguchi</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Hosokawa</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Miyamoto</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Aizawa</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Effects of ELF magnetic field on membrane protein structure of living HeLa cells studied by Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy.</article-title><source>Bioelectromagnetics</source><volume>24</volume><fpage>457</fpage><lpage>464</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12955750</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pon